>
False. They just give teleportation, never teleport control.

>  Brown pudding will give you poison resistance.
>
Actually puddings (black and brown) can give various resistances.

>  Dragons:
>    black -- disintegration resistance
>    blue -- shock resistance
>    orange -- sleep resistance
>
Generally dragon gives resistance to its breath weapon - exceptions are
yellow and gray dragons.

>That's all I can think of off-hand.  I make it a point to eat monsters
>regularly, but it's not altogether safe before you're poison resistant. 
>Stay away from yellow and violet molds unless you like to hallucinate.
>
I think yellow molds just stun you (as do bats).

Generally if you have poison resistance then experimentation is reasonably
safe. Just be sure you don't eat humans (elves if you are an elf).
Remember that corpses of low-level mosters do not always give intrinsics
- you have to eat a number of them to be sure. Plus, it is difficult to
find out what gives poison res. this way (first experiment with poison res
to find what is non-poisonous, then without it to see which non-poisonous
monsters can give poison resistance).
